<%#
  Override of redmine_reporter's app/views/my/blocks/_report_by_issues.erb.

  Carries the performance fix: feed the report a lazy AR relation
  (query.base_scope) instead of query.issues, which materialises every issue
  into memory. This override wins over the vendor partial because
  redmine_reporter_dashboards sorts after redmine_reporter in the plugin view
  load path. If the vendor rewrites this partial, revisit this override.

  --- AND IT CARRIES THE GUARD, because THIS FILE is what registers the block ---

  Redmine core discovers my-page blocks by globbing plugin view directories
  (`Redmine::MyPage.additional_blocks`), so the existence of this file makes this
  plugin contribute a core my-page block on EVERY install. Core's
  `MyHelper#render_block_content` then rescues only `ActionView::MissingTemplate`,
  so a `NameError` from naming a reporter constant here does not degrade the
  widget — it returns 500 for `/my/page`, the one page from which the user could
  otherwise remove the block.

  Two configurations reach that: standalone (no redmine_reporter at all), and
  Redmine 7.0 WITH redmine_reporter, whose report-template classes use the
  keyword form of `enum` that Rails 8.0 removed. Deleting this override fixes
  neither, because core would then glob reporter's own partial, which makes the
  same unguarded call. The guard has to be here, in the file that wins the view
  load path. Covered by test/integration/reporter_dashboards_my_page_block_test.rb.

  The placeholder is deliberately NOT nil: `MyHelper#render_block` wraps a block
  only `if content.present?`, so a widget that renders as nothing loses the
  contextual controls that carry its own close button, and the user is left with
  a block they can no longer remove.

  --- AND THE PRE-CHECK IS NOT ENOUGH ON ITS OWN ---

  The first version of this guard was `usable?` alone, and an independent review
  proved /my/page still returned 500 with `usable?` answering TRUE. Resolving the
  constants says nothing about the three other base-plugin-owned things this body
  needs: its TABLES (`find_by` against an unmigrated schema), its ROUTE HELPER
  (`report_content_report_template_path`, used by `my/report` and defined by the
  base plugin, not here), and its PARTIAL (`my/report_settings`, which this plugin
  does not ship). Measured: tables absent -> 500; partial absent -> 404, with the
  block VANISHING together with its close button, because Redmine maps
  ActionView::MissingTemplate to 404 at the controller and Rails unwraps the
  Template::Error cause — so a NESTED partial's failure escapes core's own
  block-level rescue as well.

  Hence both halves: `usable?` decides whether to try, and the rescue below is
  what makes trying safe. This is the same two-tier shape
  `reporter_project_pages_helper.rb` already uses for the project dashboard —
  a named condition degrades quietly, an arbitrary exception is logged loudly —
  rather than a second way of doing one thing.

  Nothing is appended to the output buffer before the rescue: the only writes in
  the guarded body are the `<%= render %>` calls, and `render` builds its result
  before returning, so a raise inside one leaves the buffer untouched and the
  placeholder is not appended to half a widget.
%>
<% if RedmineReporterDashboards::ReporterReportTemplates.usable?('IssueListReportTemplate') %>
  <% begin %>
    <%
      block ||= 'report_by_issues'
      settings ||= User.current.pref.my_page_settings(block) # The settings variable not defined in Redmine versions < 3.4
      query = IssueQuery.visible.find_by(id: settings[:query_id])
      report_template = IssueListReportTemplate.find_by(id: settings[:report_template_id])
    %>

    <% if query && report_template %>
      <%= render partial: 'my/report', locals: { block: block, settings: settings, query: query, collection: query.base_scope, report_template: report_template } %>
    <% else %>
      <%= render partial: 'my/report_settings',
                 locals: { block: block, settings: settings, queries: IssueQuery.visible, report_templates: IssueListReportTemplate.all } %>
    <% end %>
  <% rescue StandardError, ScriptError => e %>
    <% RedmineReporterDashboards::ReporterReportTemplates.log_render_failure(e) %>
    <p class="nodata"><%= l(:error_reporter_widget_render_failed) %></p>
  <% end %>
<% elsif RedmineReporterDashboards.reporter_present? %>
  <p class="nodata"><%= l(:error_reporter_widget_render_failed) %></p>
<% else %>
  <p class="nodata"><%= l(:text_reporter_widget_requires_plugin, plugin: RedmineReporterDashboards::ReporterPresence::PLUGIN_ID.to_s) %></p>
<% end %>
